{"name":"Radar","hex":"#b6c8e4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"radar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In full primary radar: a method of detecting a distant object and determining its position, velocity, or other characteristics by analysing radio waves (usually microwaves) which are sent towards the object and which reflect off its surfaces; also, the field of study of this method.","In full secondary radar: a method of detecting a distant object and determining its position, velocity, or other characteristics by analysing signals transmitted by the object in response to radio waves sent towards the object."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To use a radar apparatus (noun senses 1, 1.1, or 2) on (someone or something); to scan (someone or something) with, or as if with, radar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Radar","blocks":[{"text":"Radar is a system that uses radio waves to determine the distance (ranging), direction, and radial velocity of objects relative to the site. It is a radiodetermination method used to detect and track aircraft, ships, spacecraft, guided missiles, motor vehicles, weather formations and terrain. The term RADAR was coined in 1940 by the United States Navy as an acronym for \"radio detection and ranging\". The term radar has since entered English and other languages as an anacronym, a common noun, losing all capitalization."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Radar_antenna.jpg/330px-Radar_antenna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radar","wikidata":"Q47528"},{"title":"Radar (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Radar\" is a song recorded by American singer Britney Spears for her fifth studio album Blackout (2007). It was written by the Clutch and Henrik Jonback, and produced by Bloodshy & Avant and the Clutch. The recording sessions took place the day after Spears filed for divorce from Kevin Federline, and members of the Clutch claimed to be surprised by her work ethic. \"Radar\" was originally planned to be released as the third single from Blackout, but \"Break the Ice\" was chosen instead. The song was then planned as the fourth single, but the release was cancelled as Spears began recording her sixth studio album, Circus (2008). \"Radar\" was later included on Circus, and officially released as the fourth and final single from the album on June 22, 2009, by Jive Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/35/Britney_Radar.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radar_(song)","wikidata":"Q837710"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Radar-hatzerim-1-1.jpg/500px-Radar-hatzerim-1-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Radar-hatzerim-1-1.jpg/1280px-Radar-hatzerim-1-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Radar-hatzerim-1-1.jpg/500px-Radar-hatzerim-1-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARadar-hatzerim-1-1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Early_radar_antenna_-_US_Naval_Research_Laboratory_Anacostia.jpg/500px-Early_radar_antenna_-_US_Naval_Research_Laboratory_Anacostia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Early_radar_antenna_-_US_Naval_Research_Laboratory_Anacostia.jpg/500px-Early_radar_antenna_-_US_Naval_Research_Laboratory_Anacostia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Experimental radar antenna, US N